 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: the old spelling \"Thiere\", \"Papageno's\" with an apostrophe, and the repeats of the music (\"holde Flöte\", \"nur Pamina bleibt davon\", \"Pamina\", \"höre\", \"Umsonst\", \"wo\", \"vielleicht\", \"führt mich der Ton zu ihr\"), sung as the print has them. The second time, the line ends on \"Freude…\": the word \"fühlen\", printed above the staff in bar 28 with a footnote saying it is missing in the full score, is not sung. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
